
Assignment: OOP (Constructor + Polymorphism + Overriding)

Program 1: Constructor Behavior & Default Values
Use the given student_database class:
    
class student_database: 
    name = "Unknown" 
    course = "Python" 
    
    def __init__(self,named="newname",courses="newcourses"): 
        self.name = named 
        name self.course = courses
        
Tasks:
    Create 4 objects:
        - 3 with values
        - 1 without values


    Print:
    name and course of all students


Questions:
What values does the 4th object get?
Why does it not fail?

